// Package service holds this service's business logic. It is the layer that
// decides things.
//
// Belongs here: domain types, business rules and the validation of them,
// orchestration across repositories, and the repository *interfaces* this
// package defines for its own use. The interface is owned by the consumer,
// not by the implementation.
//
// Does NOT belong here: net/http types, request or response structs, status
// codes, SQL, driver types, or anything named after a wire format. This
// layer takes plain Go values in and returns plain Go values and errors out.
// If a change here would break when the transport changes, the layering is
// wrong.
//
// Errors returned from here are the domain taxonomy in internal/apierror.
// The transport maps a category to a status code; this package never does.
//
// Empty until Mint chunk 07, which threads an example resource through all
// three layers.
package service
